    "q-275963": {
      "dom_id": "step-q275963",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\" height=\"70px\" align=\"center\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-2 \\\\ 2-2 \\\\ 2-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
